      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kimball_Junction"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town sits at 6,400 feet, about one‑half mile above sea level, giving it a high‑altitude feel even on a sunny day.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        17,
        18
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://roadsidethoughts.com/ut/kimball-junction-xx-summit-profile.htm"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Kimball Junction serves as a gateway to Park City, lying at the junction of Interstate 80 and State Route 224.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7,
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kimball_Junction"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Just beyond the town borders the 1,200‑acre Swaner Preserve and Ecocenter, a wildlife refuge that hosts diverse mountain fauna.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12,
        14
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kimball_Junction"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The original Kimball Stage Stop was a bustling hub in the late 1800s, reflecting the town’s early role in regional travel.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
